# Battleship Lab Development Rules

- Read docs/Readme.docx as the authoritative game specification.
- Implement features incrementally.
- Prefer simple, efficient Python implementations.
- Reuse existing code. Never rewrite working modules unnecessarily.
- Do not add features outside the requested scope.
- Run relevant automated tests after changes.
- Fix failures before reporting completion.
- Keep responses under 150 words.
- Report only changed files, test results, and blockers.
- Do not paste full source files into chat.
- Do not fabricate benchmark results.
- Use no paid AI APIs.
- Keep official and approximate simulation results clearly distinguished.
- Preserve compatibility with MyBot(Bot) and on_state(state).
- Use Windows-compatible commands and startup scripts.
- Ask only when an essential requirement is missing.
